2094
01:34:39.900 --> 01:34:43.780
So maybe once the masters kick in it'll rejuvenate

2095
01:34:43.780 --> 01:34:46.740
my career and you'll see me out there

2096
01:34:46.740 --> 01:34:49.163
cranking with everybody else.

2097
01:34:49.163 --> 01:34:50.500
But I do think if you're being honest,

2098
01:34:50.500 --> 01:34:53.030
something perhaps you're shrouding or to look at,

2099
01:34:53.030 --> 01:34:56.100
and maybe I'm completely off base is a fear

2100
01:34:56.100 --> 01:34:58.500
that you have that if you were

2101
01:34:58.500 --> 01:35:01.110
to dip your toe back into it,

2102
01:35:01.110 --> 01:35:03.390
that knowing yourself,

2103
01:35:03.390 --> 01:35:07.190
it could become all consuming and a distraction

2104
01:35:07.190 --> 01:35:09.482
from the things that you currently care about.

2105
01:35:09.482 --> 01:35:12.800
But that is the opportunity for growth also.

2106
01:35:12.800 --> 01:35:17.460
Can you go back into it and not succumb to that?

2107
01:35:17.460 --> 01:35:19.330
I think you're 100% correct.

2108
01:35:19.330 --> 01:35:21.970
I mean, I think that's in there because like,

2109
01:35:21.970 --> 01:35:25.620
again, it was so much part of my identity.

2110
01:35:25.620 --> 01:35:29.500
And so much of who I was or am that,

2111
01:35:29.500 --> 01:35:32.140
of course there's that fear of like, well,

2112
01:35:32.140 --> 01:35:35.290
what would happen if I just like started training a lot?

2113
01:35:35.290 --> 01:35:36.520
Would I go down that path

2114
01:35:36.520 --> 01:35:39.300
where I was kind of obsessive about it?

2115
01:35:39.300 --> 01:35:40.840
And I like to think of like,

2116
01:35:40.840 --> 01:35:43.180
of course not like I'm older, I'm wise.

2117
01:35:43.180 --> 01:35:45.200
Well, there's a little denial there, right.

2118
01:35:45.200 --> 01:35:48.180
Because you're like, yeah, that might happen.

2119
01:35:48.180 --> 01:35:50.230
So I'm just gonna pretend that doesn't exist

2120
01:35:50.230 --> 01:35:52.420
and tell everyone that I'm really happy in my life.

2121
01:35:52.420 --> 01:35:55.870
And I do it for the joy, when it in truth,

2122
01:35:55.870 --> 01:35:59.610
there's like a weird dark shadow over here

2123
01:35:59.610 --> 01:36:01.060
that as long as you don't go there,

2124
01:36:01.060 --> 01:36:02.230
you don't really have to,

2125
01:36:02.230 --> 01:36:04.180
you don't have to reckon with it.

2126
01:36:04.180 --> 01:36:05.705
Yeah.

2127
01:36:05.705 --> 01:36:07.270
No, I, 100%.

2128
01:36:07.270 --> 01:36:08.960
I 100% agree.

2129
01:36:08.960 --> 01:36:11.350
I think there there's definitely that there.

2130
01:36:11.350 --> 01:36:15.390
Well, let's move to the second pillar,

2131
01:36:15.390 --> 01:36:18.150
which is all about listening to your body.

2132
01:36:18.150 --> 01:36:19.170
I love this one.

2133
01:36:19.170 --> 01:36:20.003
Yeah.

2134
01:36:20.003 --> 01:36:21.780
So I think this is again,

2135
01:36:21.780 --> 01:36:24.400
one of those really important ones that we get backwards,

2136
01:36:24.400 --> 01:36:25.710
'cause we often get told like,

2137
01:36:25.710 --> 01:36:28.820
hey ignore your feelings, et cetera, et cetera.

2138
01:36:28.820 --> 01:36:31.563
But if you look at the science and the research,

2139
01:36:32.570 --> 01:36:34.410
your feelings and emotions

2140
01:36:35.282 --> 01:36:37.710
are almost like a messaging system.

2141
01:36:37.710 --> 01:36:42.250
It tells us what's going on inside because there's no other

2142
01:36:42.250 --> 01:36:44.640
way to like communicate that from

2143
01:36:44.640 --> 01:36:47.490
like our muscles, brain, et cetera,

2144
01:36:47.490 --> 01:36:49.580
to our conscious awareness so our feelings

2145
01:36:49.580 --> 01:36:51.870
and emotions kind of send that signal

2146
01:36:51.870 --> 01:36:53.580
and give us something to do.

2147
01:36:53.580 --> 01:36:56.210
But the key here is we gotta be able

2148
01:36:56.210 --> 01:36:57.720
to like communicate with it.

2149
01:36:57.720 --> 01:37:00.500
We gotta be able to speak its language.

2150
01:37:00.500 --> 01:37:02.350
And the athlete example, I like to give,

2151
01:37:02.350 --> 01:37:04.050
which we all understand is that

2152
01:37:05.070 --> 01:37:06.240
as an athlete early on,

2153
01:37:06.240 --> 01:37:10.900
you have to learn what is a pain that signals injury

2154
01:37:10.900 --> 01:37:12.740
and what is a pain that signals,

2155
01:37:12.740 --> 01:37:14.270
oh, that's just like some soreness

2156
01:37:14.270 --> 01:37:16.550
and it'll go away and I'll be alright.

2157
01:37:16.550 --> 01:37:18.140
The same thing applies to every

2158
01:37:18.140 --> 01:37:20.560
other kind of emotion and feeling.

2159
01:37:20.560 --> 01:37:23.010
And my wife is an elementary school teacher

2160
01:37:25.877 --> 01:37:28.390
and she conveyed this great story that she said

2161
01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:34.220
her kids who are throwing tantrums always

2162
01:37:34.220 --> 01:37:37.073
like describe them with like a singular emotion.

2163
01:37:37.920 --> 01:37:38.970
And it's very simple.

2164
01:37:38.970 --> 01:37:42.090
It's like, I'm sad, right?

2165
01:37:42.090 --> 01:37:42.923
Why?

2166
01:37:42.923 --> 01:37:44.630
Because they don't have the vocabulary

2167
01:37:44.630 --> 01:37:48.760
or the understanding to break apart what that sadness is,

2168
01:37:48.760 --> 01:37:50.830
whether it was frustration,

2169
01:37:50.830 --> 01:37:53.930
whether it was insecurity driven, whatever,

2170
01:37:53.930 --> 01:37:58.270
it has this myriad of things, they have to grow and develop

2171
01:37:58.270 --> 01:38:00.500
that vocabulary to give them context.

2172
01:38:00.500 --> 01:38:02.710
And if they do that, then they can't,

2173
01:38:02.710 --> 01:38:03.783
they can handle it,

2174
01:38:04.708 --> 01:38:07.890
when it's just like all these billions of emotions,

2175
01:38:07.890 --> 01:38:10.820
all funnel into this one word, one understanding,

2176
01:38:10.820 --> 01:38:13.349
of course they're gonna throw a temper tantrum.

2177
01:38:13.349 --> 01:38:15.600
'Cause they can't make sense of it.

2178
01:38:15.600 --> 01:38:19.770
But in this process and using athletics as an example,

2179
01:38:19.770 --> 01:38:24.770
there is a connection, an integration that takes place

2180
01:38:25.560 --> 01:38:28.470
with experience where you learn over time,

2181
01:38:28.470 --> 01:38:30.870
how to discern the difference between the niggle

2182
01:38:32.307 --> 01:38:35.623
and the injury that requires you to stop and attend to it.

2183
01:38:37.120 --> 01:38:39.170
And what's interesting and kind of ironic

2184
01:38:39.170 --> 01:38:44.030
about that is athletes become so good at

2185
01:38:44.030 --> 01:38:46.810
and so attuned to what their body is telling them.

2186
01:38:46.810 --> 01:38:48.690
Like, I can remember as a swimmer,

2187
01:38:48.690 --> 01:38:50.010
I didn't need to look at the pace clock

2188
01:38:50.010 --> 01:38:51.120
if we were doing a set of a hundred,

2189
01:38:51.120 --> 01:38:52.850
it's like, I knew exactly what my heart rate was.

2190
01:38:52.850 --> 01:38:55.370
And I knew exactly when my finger hit the wall,

2191
01:38:55.370 --> 01:38:58.190
like what my interval, like what, what time I did,

2192
01:38:58.190 --> 01:39:00.223
because you're so in touch with that.

2193
01:39:02.229 --> 01:39:05.097
But the problem with that is that

2194
01:39:07.660 --> 01:39:10.600
despite all of that athletes can be expert

2195
01:39:10.600 --> 01:39:12.200
at ignoring those signals.

2196
01:39:12.200 --> 01:39:14.860
Like I'm feeling run down,

2197
01:39:14.860 --> 01:39:17.443
I should probably, like wisdom would say like,

2198
01:39:18.356 --> 01:39:20.010
you should like take the foot off the gas,

2199
01:39:20.010 --> 01:39:22.130
but it's like, no, I need to do more.

2200
01:39:22.130 --> 01:39:23.210
I need to push through this

2201
01:39:23.210 --> 01:39:27.514
so I don't feel this way or I'm not fit or they won't taper

2202
01:39:27.514 --> 01:39:29.430
or they insist on you talk about this in the book too,

2203
01:39:29.430 --> 01:39:32.610
like, running a whole bunch before a race

2204
01:39:32.610 --> 01:39:35.460
or things like that that are driven out of insecurity.

2205
01:39:35.460 --> 01:39:36.933
Yeah.

2206
01:39:36.933 --> 01:39:37.766
So it's not only,

2207
01:39:37.766 --> 01:39:40.950
you have to be able to like communicate the same language,

2208
01:39:40.950 --> 01:39:43.270
but then you have to have like

2209
01:39:43.270 --> 01:39:46.710
the security or the quiet confidence

2210
01:39:46.710 --> 01:39:50.270
to be able to listen to what that says.

2211
01:39:50.270 --> 01:39:52.840
And I think that's where the expertise comes in,

2212
01:39:52.840 --> 01:39:54.640
is it's not just being able to,

2213
01:39:54.640 --> 01:39:55.930
oh, I'm listening to my body.

2214
01:39:55.930 --> 01:39:57.740
My body tells me this.

2215
01:39:57.740 --> 01:40:02.210
No, you've got to be able to discern like what's real.

2216
01:40:02.210 --> 01:40:04.950
And then what's what I'll just call fake,

2217
01:40:04.950 --> 01:40:07.680
and then security right from,

2218
01:40:07.680 --> 01:40:09.900
oh, I don't want a taper because like,

2219
01:40:09.900 --> 01:40:12.320
I'll feel like I'm training less and I'm losing fitness.

2220
01:40:12.320 --> 01:40:14.010
Well, you're not gonna lose fitness in a week.

2221
01:40:14.010 --> 01:40:15.775
It's not gonna happen.

2222
01:40:15.775 --> 01:40:18.300
So it can't physiologically happen.

2223
01:40:18.300 --> 01:40:19.450
That's the fake part.

2224
01:40:19.450 --> 01:40:21.610
That's the insecurity talking.

2225
01:40:21.610 --> 01:40:25.210
So you've really gotta like meld this, listen to your body,

2226
01:40:25.210 --> 01:40:27.900
plus this confidence to be able to discern

2227
01:40:27.900 --> 01:40:29.910
like what's true and what's not.

2228
01:40:29.910 --> 01:40:30.950
And that puts the lie

2229
01:40:30.950 --> 01:40:32.980
to the traditional idea of toughness.

2230
01:40:32.980 --> 01:40:35.174
Like that idea would be like,

2231
01:40:35.174 --> 01:40:37.560
I just train harder than everyone,

2232
01:40:37.560 --> 01:40:40.470
but if that's coming from a place of insecurity,

2233
01:40:40.470 --> 01:40:42.090
because you're afraid of taking

2234
01:40:42.090 --> 01:40:44.760
a day off or allowing your body to heal,

2235
01:40:44.760 --> 01:40:46.450
then that's not tough at all.

2236
01:40:46.450 --> 01:40:48.286
That's just ignorant.

2237
01:40:48.286 --> 01:40:51.030
I always like to put it as does

2238
01:40:51.030 --> 01:40:54.360
the thing have the power or are you in control?

2239
01:40:54.360 --> 01:40:56.323
And so much of toughness is like,

2240
01:40:57.310 --> 01:41:00.163
do I have some semblance of control over things,

2241
01:41:01.500 --> 01:41:02.710
not complete control,

2242
01:41:02.710 --> 01:41:05.400
but some semblance where I can influence it.

2243
01:41:05.400 --> 01:41:07.940
So if the thing has all the control,

2244
01:41:07.940 --> 01:41:11.510
if I can't step away from the run, say, hey, you know what,

2245
01:41:11.510 --> 01:41:13.690
I'm a little sick and I've got a race coming up.

2246
01:41:13.690 --> 01:41:15.720
So it's probably better that I rest.

2247
01:41:15.720 --> 01:41:18.080
If I can't do that without like

2248
01:41:18.080 --> 01:41:19.713
that anxiety coming up,

2249
01:41:20.730 --> 01:41:22.370
that should signal

2250
01:41:22.370 --> 01:41:26.640
it's an issue that I need to be able to work with to sit

2251
01:41:26.640 --> 01:41:28.540
with that discomfort so that

2252
01:41:28.540 --> 01:41:30.620
the thing doesn't have the control.

2253
01:41:30.620 --> 01:41:32.960
And instead I'm making the wise decision

2254
01:41:32.960 --> 01:41:34.270
and taking the action.

2255
01:41:34.270 --> 01:41:37.580
And the coach or the mentor, or the leader,

2256
01:41:37.580 --> 01:41:40.810
has to understand how to instill that in the people

2257
01:41:40.810 --> 01:41:42.190
that they're working with.

2258
01:41:42.190 --> 01:41:44.020
So that's the difference between

2259
01:41:45.550 --> 01:41:47.490
the controlling Bobby Knights out there

2260
01:41:47.490 --> 01:41:49.580
who strip their athletes

2261
01:41:49.580 --> 01:41:53.650
of any agency or control versus the empowering coach

2262
01:41:53.650 --> 01:41:57.500
who understands how to kind of seed

2263
01:41:57.500 --> 01:41:59.380
that intrinsic motivation

2264
01:41:59.380 --> 01:42:02.220
and that true confidence where

2265
01:42:02.220 --> 01:42:06.160
the athlete or the mentee is empowered to make

2266
01:42:06.160 --> 01:42:07.930
their own decisions and feels like they

2267
01:42:07.930 --> 01:42:11.530
have input into the trajectory of their career.

2268
01:42:11.530 --> 01:42:16.120
The easiest way to make an athlete worse

2269
01:42:16.120 --> 01:42:19.487
is to take away autonomy because like-

2270
01:42:19.487 --> 01:42:21.150
And you think that goes back

2271
01:42:21.150 --> 01:42:22.870
to the traditional versus the truth.

2272
01:42:22.870 --> 01:42:24.770
Like if you just tell like,

2273
01:42:24.770 --> 01:42:27.130
this is what you, do what I say,

2274
01:42:27.130 --> 01:42:28.680
I'm gonna make you a champion.

2275
01:42:28.680 --> 01:42:31.680
I will completely control every aspect of your life.

2276
01:42:31.680 --> 01:42:34.810
Like I don't know Bela Carole and these gymnasts,

2277
01:42:34.810 --> 01:42:37.833
or you hear all these crazy examples and you know,

2278
01:42:37.833 --> 01:42:39.810
they're successful in some regard,

2279
01:42:39.810 --> 01:42:43.210
those people don't tend to turn out to be completely

2280
01:42:44.117 --> 01:42:47.050
well rounded individuals,

2281
01:42:47.050 --> 01:42:49.810
but there are examples of that being successful.

2282
01:42:49.810 --> 01:42:52.530
And yet that's really a wrongheaded approach.

2283
01:42:52.530 --> 01:42:54.660
Yeah, because it's all it's doing

2284
01:42:54.660 --> 01:42:56.260
is you're not training anything.

2285
01:42:57.410 --> 01:43:00.260
You're training someone to respond

2286
01:43:00.260 --> 01:43:04.460
to this single individual based on fear or punishment.

2287
01:43:04.460 --> 01:43:08.060
But if you look at most sports,

2288
01:43:08.060 --> 01:43:10.220
like it's not the coach isn't out there

2289
01:43:10.220 --> 01:43:11.940
with the athlete on top of them yelling

2290
01:43:11.940 --> 01:43:13.580
and screaming and doing all that stuff.

2291
01:43:13.580 --> 01:43:16.420
It's the athlete out there by themselves,

2292
01:43:16.420 --> 01:43:19.180
in their head having to figure it out.

2293
01:43:19.180 --> 01:43:20.946
If we take it outside of sport,

2294
01:43:20.946 --> 01:43:23.130
like you're not worried about

2295
01:43:23.130 --> 01:43:26.540
what your kids do when you look over them.

2296
01:43:26.540 --> 01:43:27.620
When you're there in the house.

2297
01:43:27.620 --> 01:43:29.240
You're worried about what happens

2298
01:43:29.240 --> 01:43:32.350
when they go out into the world, same in the workplace.

2299
01:43:32.350 --> 01:43:35.960
So to me, it's pretty simple as like, yeah,

2300
01:43:35.960 --> 01:43:39.860
that like dictating and controlling method might work

2301
01:43:39.860 --> 01:43:42.640
if you're right over the top of them,

2302
01:43:42.640 --> 01:43:44.280
but you wanna train the ability.

2303
01:43:44.280 --> 01:43:47.490
And in order to do that, you have to give them a choice.

2304
01:43:47.490 --> 01:43:50.109
My favorite example in the book of that

2305
01:43:50.109 --> 01:43:53.700
is what Kerr does with the warriors

2306
01:43:53.700 --> 01:43:55.330
when they're at the top of their game

2307
01:43:55.330 --> 01:43:56.540
and they're winning everything.

2308
01:43:56.540 --> 01:43:58.390
So tell that story.

2309
01:43:58.390 --> 01:43:59.420
I think it's very instructive.

2310
01:43:59.420 --> 01:44:03.600
So it's the middle of one of their championship seasons.

2311
01:44:03.600 --> 01:44:06.520
And they were winning a lot.

2312
01:44:06.520 --> 01:44:09.030
They were one of the best teams obviously.

2313
01:44:09.030 --> 01:44:11.290
And he looks around and he says, you know what?

2314
01:44:11.290 --> 01:44:14.760
Like, ah, we're lacking a little something.

2315
01:44:14.760 --> 01:44:16.890
So he goes in the pregame,

2316
01:44:16.890 --> 01:44:19.290
like shoot around in the morning and says, guys,

2317
01:44:20.170 --> 01:44:22.810
you're gonna coach, I'm gonna step back.

2318
01:44:22.810 --> 01:44:25.246
You run the practice,

2319
01:44:25.246 --> 01:44:26.410
you run the game,

2320
01:44:26.410 --> 01:44:27.880
you call everything.

2321
01:44:27.880 --> 01:44:30.570
I'm gonna step back. And he just hands over the reins.

2322
01:44:30.570 --> 01:44:32.850
Has anybody ever done that in the NBA before?

2323
01:44:32.850 --> 01:44:34.270
I don't think in the NBA.

2324
01:44:34.270 --> 01:44:37.500
There wasn't an example that I could find of just turning it

2325
01:44:37.500 --> 01:44:40.360
over to literally players, not player coaches,

2326
01:44:40.360 --> 01:44:42.920
literally players to call it.

2327
01:44:42.920 --> 01:44:44.790
But I think that's such an empowering thing

2328
01:44:44.790 --> 01:44:47.570
because what message does it send?

2329
01:44:47.570 --> 01:44:51.130
I trust you and it's up to you.

2330
01:44:51.130 --> 01:44:52.120
Yeah.

2331
01:44:52.120 --> 01:44:53.850
Which is the best of both worlds.

2332
01:44:53.850 --> 01:44:55.520
It's saying, I trust you.

2333
01:44:55.520 --> 01:45:00.010
I have my faith in you and you guys go show me, you got it.

2334
01:45:00.010 --> 01:45:01.590
You guys get the work done.

2335
01:45:01.590 --> 01:45:03.810
Like I have the confidence in you.

2336
01:45:03.810 --> 01:45:07.600
You wanna talk about in instilling trust and confidence.

2337
01:45:07.600 --> 01:45:09.223
That's how you do it.

2338
01:45:10.380 --> 01:45:12.030
Because that's real,

2339
01:45:12.030 --> 01:45:13.960
that's turning over those reins.

2340
01:45:13.960 --> 01:45:17.720
That's saying, hey, I believe in you guys.

2341
01:45:17.720 --> 01:45:20.090
And let's see what you guys can do.

2342
01:45:20.090 --> 01:45:21.910
I'm gonna give you the shot.

2343
01:45:21.910 --> 01:45:23.280
And so in the workplace,

2344
01:45:23.280 --> 01:45:28.186
the analogy would be stop micromanaging and find ways

2345
01:45:28.186 --> 01:45:29.040
to incentivize the people

2346
01:45:29.040 --> 01:45:30.590
that are working underneath you

2347
01:45:31.672 --> 01:45:35.590
and provide them with agency to make decisions and choices.

2348
01:45:35.590 --> 01:45:37.800
Which goes against our natural

2349
01:45:37.800 --> 01:45:39.650
inclination when things are tough.

2350
01:45:39.650 --> 01:45:41.983
And when things are going difficult.

2351
01:45:43.170 --> 01:45:44.690
